          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On October 21, 1954, at 7:30 PM, two gendarmes observed for a maximum of 15 seconds a very bright, glowing streak that silently crossed the sky at high speed in a north-south direction. In the dark night with a clear sky and visible stars, this streak had the shape of a cone with the point forward and the base extended by numerous sparks. Its trajectory was horizontal. Although the witnesses (incorrectly) ruled out a meteor \"due to the importance of its dimensions and the horizontality of its trajectory,\" what they likely saw was a meteoroid entering the atmosphere and fragmenting. The GEIPAN classifies this case as B: probable observation of the passage of a bolide caused by the atmospheric entry of a natural meteoroid that fragments.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "df3c9bea3d1bc3e73d305f7776f884f8d9ccc95b1e63333ae71e083acee8647e"
        }
